TMDA and postfix integration
=====

Incoming messages
-----

For incoming messages, TMDA should be hooked in via postfix' configured Mail Delivery Agent (MDA).

### Procmail

In one's ~/.procmailrc:

# Catch/verify TMDA-related messages
# NOTE: with the '-p' option (used along :f procmail recipe), valid messages will
#       NOT be delivered by TMDA itself but further processed by procmail
:0 fW
* ^(Delivered-)?To:.*cdufour-(confirm|dated|sender|keyword)-
| /usr/bin/tmda-filter -p
:0 e
/dev/null


Outgoing messages
-----

TMDA historically depends on tmda-ofmipd as mail submission daemon - as a frontend to tmda-inject -
to tag outgoing messages and/or append recipient addresses to some whitelist.

With Python asynchat module being planned for removal in Python 3.12 (and significant refactoring
beeing needed to port it to asyncio), one may want to hook tmda-inject directly into postfix.

Example given using the SMTPS (TCP/465) port; in /etc/postfix/master.cf:

smtps inet n       -       y       -       -       smtpd
  -o syslog_name=postfix/smtps
  -o smtpd_tls_wrappermode=yes
  -o smtpd_sasl_auth_enable=yes
  -o content_filter=tmda-inject:
tmda-inject  unix  -       n       n       -       -       pipe
  flags=R user=mail argv=/etc/postfix/tmda-submission ${sasl_username} ${recipient}

And the tmda-submission script:

#!/bin/sh
export USER=${1%%@*}
export HOME=/data/users/${USER}
shift

exec /usr/bin/tmda-inject -c "${HOME}/.tmda/config" "${@}"
